# The primitive table of the translator (§GATE "all settings in tables", slice 2; Q36, Q41;
# steps/table-receiver.md §7): lingvamyxa_prev's `primitive.description` (lm2/primitive.lm2), its columns and
# rows verbatim.  The translator reads the columns class, cell and convert (l2_prim_kind): a row names a
# primitive, `cell` 1 is a cell primitive, `convert` forbidden forbids a conversion to or from it.
# The rows are the 23 names the translator knew before this table; the other rows of lingvamyxa_prev are not
# taken yet -- taking them is a data step with its own measurement (steps/table-receiver.md §7):
# Cell Count Integer Flag Ratio Float Complex Atom Address Opaque Text llong flong signed uchar ushort ullong usize isize categoryFlag uint8 int8 f32 f64 bigint real decimal DecimalText.
# Where the translator's tables live is open (Q46); until then this file is read beside the source, as
# convert.lm2 is.
table:
    source
    name: `primitive.description`
    columns: (class: class) (categoryFlag: cell) (class: semantic) (categoryFlag: numeric) (categoryFlag: integer) (categoryFlag: floating) (categoryFlag: reference) (categoryFlag: opaque) (categoryFlag: callable) (categoryFlag: descriptor) (categoryFlag: signed) (class: width) (class: range) (class: spelling) (class: convert)
